sg-session (0.1.0-42) unstable; urgency=medium

  * sg-domain-logon: a domain user's Windows identity from winbind at
    sign-in -- /run/stained-glass/domain-sids/<uid> (SID, primary and domain
    groups, the domain's well-known groups by name), which wine-sg 0205
    turns into their SID, groups and names on the Windows side -- and
    ProfileList\<SID> in the machine's registry.
  * Machine Group Policy: computer startup scripts (a GPO's
    Machine\Scripts\scripts.ini [Startup]) fetched with the machine account
    and run once per boot as SYSTEM; sg-gpupdate.service applies the
    computer's policy at boot, not only from the 90-minute timer.
  * sg-sid-probe.exe, the domain gate's Windows identity probe.
  * Breaks wine-sg << 10.0-61: before its 0211 a domain user's session
    left display keys the login screen could not delete, and it spun.

