sg-session (0.1.0-40) unstable; urgency=medium

  * B56: an elevated program gets a display of its own. sg-brokerd execs
    the new sg-elevated-run (as SYSTEM) after consent: an Xwayland run as
    SYSTEM that admits only its cookie, handed to the requester's
    compositor (sg-compositor ELEVATED) as the window manager of its
    windows, and the program with DISPLAY/XAUTHORITY and a Wine desktop of
    its own (SG_WINSTATION WinSta0\sg-elevated-<display>); the display lives
    while the program and its children do. Never the session's display: the
    broker no longer passes the requester's DISPLAY, WAYLAND_DISPLAY,
    XAUTHORITY or runtime directory. SYSTEM's HKCU gets Decorated=N.
  * The consent prompt's and the lock screen's X servers admit only their
    own account (sg_x_cookie, -auth): without it any local account could
    connect to them. make test-consent checks it across accounts.
  * sg-lockctl: WINDOWS, and ACTIVATE <display> <window> for the taskbar.

