sg-session (0.1.0-39) unstable; urgency=medium

  * VPN connections (sg-netctl vpn): an administrator imports a vendor's
    WireGuard .conf or OpenVPN .ovpn as a NetworkManager connection for all
    users (checked first: nothing that runs a program, no file of this
    computer named, only known OpenVPN directives); anyone with a session
    lists, dials (a password on stdin, to NetworkManager in a file) and
    hangs up. Windows programs reach it through RAS (wine-sg 0400: rasdial,
    RasDial, RasEnumConnections). netctl-test covers who may do what and
    every refusal.
  * Print to PDF: sg-print-setup.service adds a CUPS queue on cups-pdf,
    the default printer unless one is chosen, writing into the user's
    Documents; every Windows program's Print dialog lists it. Unit test
    test/print-setup-test.sh; sg-print-check prints from Notepad and reads
    the PDF back (sg-image make print-test).

